        "text": "All required Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_text.py** - Extracts plain text from a scanned document image using Google Cloud Vision API.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_layout.py** - Extracts blocks, lines, tables, or layout elements from a document using Google Cloud Vision API.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_tables.py** - Extracts table cells and row structure from a document using Google Cloud Vision API.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_key_values.py** - Extracts key-value pairs from a form-like document using Google Cloud Vision API.\n5. **[HELPER] document_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for OCR and Layout Extraction.\n6. **[HELPER] document_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for OCR and Layout Extraction.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_translate.py** - Translates extracted OCR text using Google Cloud Translate API.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_safety.py** - Checks extracted document text for unsafe content using Google Cloud Vision API.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] document_field_extraction.py** - Extracts structured fields from OCR-normalized document text using Google Cloud Vision API.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_embedding.py** - Embeds extracted document sections for semantic retrieval using Google Cloud Vision API.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses the Google Cloud Vision API, making it identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
